Use fractional ideals, not an assumption of principal a_c.
Put J_c=a_(c^2)/a_c. Multiplication gives prod_c J_c=O_K exactly.
For fixed p and embedding, the actual isogeny-integrality theorem
applied to forward maps says every element of u_c J_c has norm<=1.
The inverse maps give the same assertion for u_c^-1 J_c^-1.
Products of these fractional modules are generated by finite sums
of products; the ultrametric inequality preserves integrality.
Hence U=prod_c u_c and U^-1 are both integral, giving |iota_p U|=1.
This conclusion does NOT require each u_c individually to be a unit.

